<title>SOUTH KOREA: Seoul watchdog details Housing Bank GDR issue plan.</title>
<headline>Seoul watchdog details Housing Bank GDR issue plan.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Securities Supervisory Board said on Friday foreign ownership in South Korea's Housing and Commercial Bank would rise to 49.8 percent from 23 percent after a planned global depositary receipt issue.</p>
<p>The bank, currently 46.8 percent owned by the government, plans to issue up to $300 million worth of receipts on July 22 and list them on the London Stock Exchange, the board said.</p>
<p>About half of the receipts will be issued with existing shares owned by the government as underlying shares, while the bank will issue new shares for the other half, it said.</p>
</text>
